<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarki</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarki is a historic Kumyk settlement on the Caspian coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>, now a district of the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makhachkala">Makhachkala</a>. From the 17th century until 1867 it was the seat of the shamkhals of Tarki, who controlled the coastal plain on the route between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> visited it during his Persian campaign of 1722.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tarki.jpg" alt="Tarki" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Милютин Д. А. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tarki.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
